B.hj=new A.Cz("Training",0,"training")
B.anm=new A.eP("Muscles and strength grow when training asks a little more of them over time. Doing the same weight for the same reps every week stops working after the first few months.")
B.a3J=new A.jS("How to add a little more")
B.aew=s(["More reps with the same weight, up to the top of your rep range.","Then more weight: 2.5 kg on big lifts, 1 kg on small ones, and start again at the bottom of the range.","Or one more set, when the sessions feel easy and you\u2019re recovering well."],t.s)
B.RK=new A.ij(B.aew)
B.anj=new A.eP("This is what the app does when you log workouts: it keeps the weight until every set reaches the top of the range, then suggests a small jump. The research behind it suggests raising the load by 2 to 10% once you can beat the target reps by one or two.")
B.aD1=new A.l9("Write it down. You can\u2019t beat last week if you don\u2019t know what last week was.")
B.acD=s([B.anm,B.a3J,B.RK,B.anj,B.aD1],t.Wi)
B.By=s([1],t.t)
B.Qn=new A.ht("overload","Progressive overload","The one rule every program is built on.",B.hj,B.cM,3,B.acD,B.By)
B.ani=new A.eP("Muscle grows across a wide range of reps, from about 5 to 30 a set, as long as the set ends close to failure. Heavier sets of 1 to 6 build the most strength; moderate ones (6 to 15) are the most time-efficient for size.")
B.a3G=new A.jS("Reps in reserve")
B.anA=new A.eP("Count how many more reps you could have done with good form. Ending most sets with 1 to 3 in reserve gives nearly all the benefit without grinding yourself down. Going to true failure on every set mostly adds fatigue.")
B.a3L=new A.jS("How many sets")
B.anr=new A.eP("More weekly sets per muscle generally means more growth, up to a point. Around 10 hard sets per muscle a week is a solid target; beginners grow on less.")
B.aCV=new A.l9("If a set of 10 could have been 15, it didn\u2019t count for much. Pick a weight that makes the last two reps hard.")
B.acM=s([B.ani,B.a3G,B.anA,B.a3L,B.anr,B.aCV],t.Wi)
B.a8Y=s([2,3,5],t.t)
B.Qo=new A.ht("sets-reps","Sets, reps and how hard","Rep ranges, and why the last few reps matter most.",B.hj,B.cM,4,B.acM,B.a8Y)
B.anu=new A.eP("Training each muscle twice a week tends to beat once a week for growth when the total sets are the same. That\u2019s why the plan uses full-body sessions on 2 to 3 days and upper/lower or push/pull/legs splits on 4 to 6.")
B.ahr=s(["New to lifting: 2 to 3 full-body days.","Some experience: 3 to 4 days.","Advanced: 4 to 5 days, if recovery and life allow."],t.s)
B.RF=new A.ij(B.ahr)
B.ano=new A.eP("For health, the World Health Organization recommends muscle strengthening on at least two days a week, plus 150 to 300 minutes of moderate activity such as brisk walking.")
B.aD0=new A.l9("The best split is the one you\u2019ll actually do. Three sessions every week beat five that fall apart in a month.")
B.adW=s([B.anu,B.RF,B.ano,B.aD0],t.Wi)
B.a8G=s([1,4,13],t.t)
B.Qs=new A.ht("frequency","How often to train","Twice a week per muscle, and why full body works.",B.hj,B.cM,3,B.adW,B.a8G)
B.ahS=s(["Lower the weight under control; don\u2019t drop into the bottom.","Use the full range you can control. Half reps with more weight usually build less.","Keep the same form on the last rep as the first. If it breaks down, the set is over.","Pain that is sharp or in a joint is a stop sign, not something to push through."],t.s)
B.RC=new A.ij(B.ahS)
B.a3N=new A.jS("A quick warm-up")
B.ah3=s(["3 to 5 minutes of easy movement to get warm.","For the first big lift: an empty bar or light weight for 8 to 10, then about half your working weight for 5, then three-quarters for 2 to 3.","Later exercises need one light set, if that."],t.s)
B.RE=new A.ij(B.ah3)
B.aCX=new A.l9("Film a set from the side now and then. It shows what you can\u2019t feel.")
B.ah_=s([B.RC,B.a3N,B.RE,B.aCX],t.Wi)
B.Qw=new A.ht("technique","Technique and warming up","Control, full range, and a warm-up that takes five minutes.",B.hj,B.cM,3,B.ah_,B.By)
B.anv=new A.eP("After the first year, progress comes slower and needs more planning. Three levers do most of the work: how many sets, how heavy, and how you arrange the week.")
B.a3K=new A.jS("Volume")
B.ang=new A.eP("Somewhere around 10 to 20 hard sets per muscle per week is where most trained people grow best. Add sets to a lagging muscle a few at a time, not all at once, and watch whether you recover.")
B.a3H=new A.jS("Plateaus")
B.ahH=s(["Check the basics first: sleep, food, and whether you\u2019re really adding reps or weight.","Change the rep range for a block: 4 to 6 weeks heavier, then 4 to 6 lighter.","Swap the exercise for a close variation (incline for flat bench, front squat for back squat).","Take a lighter week (see deloads) if everything feels heavy."],t.s)
B.RA=new A.ij(B.ahH)
B.a3I=new A.jS("Strength vs size")
B.anp=new A.eP("For strength, keep the main lifts heavy (1 to 6 reps) and practise them often. For size, the total hard sets matter most, and the load can vary.")
B.af7=s([B.anv,B.a3K,B.ang,B.a3H,B.RA,B.a3I,B.anp],t.Wi)
B.a8Z=s([2,4,16,1],t.t)
B.Qv=new A.ht("volume-intermediate","Volume, splits and plateaus","When the beginner gains slow down.",B.hj,B.kg,5,B.af7,B.a8Z)
B.anl=new A.eP("Your strength moves day to day with sleep, food and stress. Rating each set by reps in reserve lets the weight follow how you are, not a fixed number.")
B.aeU=s(["RIR 3: could have done three more. A good working set early in a block.","RIR 1 to 2: hard. Most working sets.","RIR 0: nothing left. Save it for the last set of an exercise, if at all, and not on the big lifts."],t.s)
B.RH=new A.ij(B.aeU)
B.ans=new A.eP("A simple plan: aim for RIR 3 in week one, 2 in week two, 1 in week three, then a lighter week. The weights rise as the target RIR falls.")
B.aCZ=new A.l9("Most people guess low at first: they had more left than they thought. Test it now and then on a safe exercise.")
B.ag_=s([B.anl,B.RH,B.ans,B.aCZ],t.Wi)
B.a9N=s([5],t.t)
B.Qq=new A.ht("rir-intermediate","Training by effort (RIR)","Using reps in reserve to choose the day\u2019s weight.",B.hj,B.kg,4,B.ag_,B.a9N)
B.iN=new A.Cz("Food",1,"food")
B.ann=new A.eP("Body weight follows energy balance over weeks: eat less than you use and you lose, more and you gain. Day-to-day weight jumps of a kilo are mostly water and food in your gut, not fat.")
B.a3E=new A.jS("Sensible speeds")
B.agk=s(["Losing fat: about 0.5 to 1% of body weight a week. Slower keeps more muscle and strength.","Building muscle: about 0.25 to 0.5% a week. Faster is mostly fat.","Recomp: hold steady or lose very slowly while training hard."],t.s)
B.RJ=new A.ij(B.agk)
B.ank=new A.eP("The app starts you from an estimate of your needs and adjusts it every two weeks from your weigh-ins, because every estimate is off for someone.")
B.aD3=new A.l9("Judge by the weekly average, not one morning. Weigh in at the same time, after waking, a few times a week.")
B.a9M=s([B.ann,B.a3E,B.RJ,B.ank,B.aD3],t.Wi)
B.aaO=s([8,9,7],t.t)
B.Qr=new A.ht("calories","Calories, simply","Why weight changes, and how fast is sensible.",B.iN,B.cM,4,B.a9M,B.aaO)
B.anz=new A.eP("Protein is the building material for muscle. For people lifting weights, about 1.6 g per kg of body weight a day captures most of the benefit; a little more (around 2 g/kg) helps hold muscle while losing fat.")
B.a3F=new A.jS("Easy sources")
B.aeX=s(["Vegetarian: paneer, curd and Greek yogurt, milk, dals and rajma or chole, soya chunks, tofu, besan, sprouts.","Eggs: about 6 g each; the whites alone are almost pure protein.","Non-veg: chicken, fish, mutton, about 25 to 30 g per 100 g cooked.","Whey: about 24 g a scoop. Handy, not necessary."],t.s)
B.RD=new A.ij(B.aeX)
B.ant=new A.eP("Dals and grains each lack something the other has; eaten together through the day (dal with rice or roti) they cover your needs. Soya and paneer are the densest vegetarian options.")
B.aD_=new A.l9("Put a protein food in every meal. Three or four meals of 25 to 40 g is easier than catching up at night.")
B.acI=s([B.anz,B.a3F,B.RD,B.ant,B.aD_],t.Wi)
B.aaz=s([6,7,15],t.t)
B.Qu=new A.ht("protein","Protein, and where to get it","How much, and Indian sources for every diet.",B.iN,B.cM,4,B.acI,B.aaz)
B.anx=new A.eP("Once protein is covered, carbs and fat fill the rest. Neither is fattening on its own; total calories decide that. Carbs fuel hard training, so lifters usually do better with a fair amount of them.")
B.acA=s(["Fat: keep at least about 0.5 to 1 g per kg a day for hormones and health. Nuts, seeds, oils, ghee in moderation.","Carbs: rice, roti, oats, millets, fruit, potatoes. Whole grains and millets keep you fuller.","Half the plate vegetables, a quarter protein, a quarter grains is a good default for most meals."],t.s)
B.RG=new A.ij(B.acA)
B.any=new A.eP("Cooking oil is where home meals hide most of their calories: a tablespoon is about 120 kcal. Measuring it for a week is an eye opener.")
B.agP=s([B.anx,B.RG,B.any],t.Wi)
B.aaV=s([9,15],t.t)
B.Qt=new A.ht("carbs-fat","Carbs, fat and a balanced plate","What fills the rest of your calories.",B.iN,B.cM,3,B.agP,B.aaV)
B.anh=new A.eP("Very few supplements have strong evidence. Food, sleep and training matter far more.")
B.aeJ=s(["Creatine monohydrate: 3 to 5 g a day, any time. Among the most studied supplements; it helps strength and muscle gain and is safe for healthy adults.","Caffeine: about 3 mg per kg, 30 to 60 minutes before training, improves performance for most people. Not late in the day.","Whey or plant protein: food in a scoop. Useful only if you can\u2019t reach your protein otherwise."],t.s)
B.RM=new A.ij(B.aeJ)
B.aD2=new A.l9("Check with a doctor first if you have a kidney or heart condition, are pregnant, or take medicine.")
B.a94=s([B.anh,B.RM,B.aD2],t.Wi)
B.a8l=s([10,11,6],t.t)
B.Qy=new A.ht("supplements","Supplements that work","Creatine, caffeine and protein powder; skip the rest.",B.iN,B.cM,3,B.a94,B.a8l)
B.anC=new A.eP("Building muscle while losing fat is realistic for beginners, people returning after a break, and those with more fat to lose. For lean, experienced lifters it is slow, and separate building and cutting phases usually work better.")
B.a3M=new A.jS("Making a recomp work")
B.acq=s(["Eat close to maintenance, or a small deficit.","Keep protein high, around 2 g per kg.","Train hard and add load or reps over time.","Judge by your waist, photos and strength, not just the scale."],t.s)
B.Rz=new A.ij(B.acq)
B.a3D=new A.jS("Diet breaks")
B.anB=new A.eP("On a long cut, a week or two at maintenance every couple of months can make it easier to stick to. It doesn\u2019t undo progress; expect the scale to bump up a little with water and food weight.")
B.adc=s([B.anC,B.a3M,B.Rz,B.a3D,B.anB],t.Wi)
B.a8p=s([14,7,8],t.t)
B.Qp=new A.ht("recomp-intermediate","Recomp and diet breaks","Losing fat and building muscle at once, and when to pause.",B.iN,B.kg,4,B.adc,B.a8p)
B.oV=new A.Cz("Recovery and progress",2,"recovery")
B.anq=new A.eP("Adults need 7 or more hours of sleep a night. Short sleep makes training feel harder, raises hunger and makes a diet harder to stick to.")
B.ai4=s(["Keep the same wake-up time, even on weekends.","No caffeine in the 6 to 8 hours before bed.","A cool, dark room; phone away from the bed.","Soreness is normal for a day or two after new exercises and fades as you get used to them. It isn\u2019t a measure of a good workout."],t.s)
B.RB=new A.ij(B.ai4)
B.adK=s([B.anq,B.RB],t.Wi)
B.a8n=s([12],t.t)
B.Ql=new A.ht("sleep","Sleep and recovery","Where the training actually turns into results.",B.oV,B.cM,3,B.adK,B.a8n)
B.aaX=s(["Scale: a few mornings a week, after the toilet, before eating. Watch the weekly average.","Waist: once a week, at the navel, relaxed. Going down while weight holds means a recomp is working.","Photos: every two to four weeks, same light and pose.","Strength: your logged lifts. Rising numbers while losing weight means you\u2019re keeping muscle."],t.s)
B.RI=new A.ij(B.aaX)
B.aCY=new A.l9("Give any change two to three weeks before judging it. Two days of data says almost nothing.")
B.a9Z=s([B.RI,B.aCY],t.Wi)
B.aaA=s([7],t.t)
B.Qm=new A.ht("measure","Measuring progress","Scale, tape, photos and the logbook.",B.oV,B.cM,3,B.a9Z,B.aaA)
B.anw=new A.eP("Fatigue builds up over weeks of hard training. A planned lighter week lets it clear so you come back stronger.")
B.abR=s(["Every 4 to 8 weeks, or when weights that were easy feel heavy for more than a session or two.","Keep the exercises; halve the sets, or drop the weight by about a tenth and stop far from failure.","Signs you need one: stalled lifts across the board, poor sleep, aching joints, dreading sessions."],t.s)
B.RL=new A.ij(B.abR)
B.aCW=new A.l9("A deload week still counts as training. Keep checking in.")
B.agy=s([B.anw,B.RL,B.aCW],t.Wi)
B.a8H=s([1,5],t.t)
B.Qx=new A.ht("deload-intermediate","Deloads and fatigue","A lighter week so the next block goes better.",B.oV,B.kg,3,B.agy,B.a8H)
B.fL=s([B.Qn,B.Qo,B.Qs,B.Qw,B.Qv,B.Qq,B.Qr,B.Qu,B.Qt,B.Qy,B.Qp,B.Ql,B.Qm,B.Qx],A.ag("D<ht>"))
